title: Settings › Agents › Which steps need a person
route: /settings
intro: The PRD guardrail matrix, step by step: what each kind of agent action may do on its own and which human step it still needs. The Settings page only hints at this in its Gates card.
dir: TD
also: From docs/prior-auth/prd/07-ai-agents-and-automation.md, section 7. The demo does not enforce any of it from this page.
---
start s1 "An agent wants to take a step"
decision q1 "What kind of step is it?"

process a1 "Auto + notify\nA person acts only on exceptions"
process a2 "Stage\nIntake confirms before the coverage change lands"
process a3 "Auto when the reading is sure\nStage when it is not, and always for a partial approval\nThe coordinator checks against the letter"
process a4 "Stage\nThe coordinator confirms before the EMR is written"
process a5 "Draft\nThe clinician edits the clinical content and signs"
process a6 "Human-initiated, after a signature\nThe clinician's signature is bound to the packet hash"
process a7 "Auto + notify, a later phase\nThe coordinator reviews the outcome"
process a8 "Human-initiated\nThe coordinator schedules, a clinician attends the peer-to-peer"
process a9 "Auto + notify\nThe operator acknowledges the proposed rule"
endx x1 "Never\nThe clinician authors clinical content and sets units, frequency and dates\nCallers never answer clinical questions"

click h1 "Clinician signs\nA licensed clinician signs every request and appeal"
click h2 "Case owner confirms the write-back"
goto g1 "Continues in: New case › Review and sign"
goto g2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Request drawer › Approve the write-back"
goto g3 "Continues in: Payers › Changes › Acknowledge a change"
goto g4 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Appeal drawer › Sign and send"

s1 --> q1
q1 -->|Read, poll or check: eligibility, packet completeness, status, decision letters| a1
q1 -->|Change coverage on the chart: Verify| a2
q1 -->|Put units, window and reason in the ledger: Navigator| a3
q1 -->|Write the approval number and dates to the EMR: Navigator| a4
q1 -->|Draft a cover sheet or an appeal letter: Packet, Advocate| a5
q1 -->|Submit, fax, email an appeal or message a payer: Navigator| a6
q1 -->|Call a payer for receipt or status: Caller| a7
q1 -->|Call a payer for denial criteria or a peer-to-peer: Caller| a8
q1 -->|Propose a payer rule from a bulletin: Sentinel, Packet, Advocate| a9
q1 -->|Write clinical content, choose units or dates, answer clinical questions| x1
a5 --> h1
a6 --> h1
a4 --> h2
h1 --> g1
h1 -.-> g4
h2 --> g2
a9 -.-> g3
